Z||000000||anna||05-21-99||06:19 PM||||I m sure that most of you had to deal with rocks hitten your cars,people using keys to scratch up your car and etc. etc...So many things can happen to your nice paint job.Like most people you use  touch up stick you by at the store.Then get mad, cause the paint don't match.I came acoss a guy ,who sell a touch up kit for cars.All he needs to know is the current paintcode from the car.He schould be able to exactly match it.I've used it on all my cars and it works great.Here is his webside.    www.ultimatetouchup.com    He is a very nice guy and wont mind answering any question.
Z||000001||theogre||05-21-99||09:34 PM||||never use a stick.... the only off the shelf thing that ever comes close is properly applied Duplicolor spray paint.
Z||000002||overlord||05-22-99||12:08 PM||||its funny, i drive all the time on gravel roads and have never had any problems with paint damage from stones...(lucky i guess)<p>but there are some spots here and there that have tiny flaws.(just weathered paint i guess).<p>so what is the best touching up item that can be used?  i was thinking of repainting the whole car (but funds are low now)
Z||000003||theogre||05-22-99||05:38 PM||||if the paint has any thru damage it can only be repaired by sanding down and repainting the afflicted area.<p>If the paint is scuffed but not cracked thru then it can be "compounded" and buffed. Sometimes you can hide damaged clear coat this way as well. (you compound off the cleat coat, and apply a good wax, in the damaged area. It's very tedious, and you have to be carefull not to go thru the base color.)
Z||000004||Punkndrublic||05-24-99||03:48 PM||||Why not paint the car with paint from Endura Pacific? I used paint from them to paint my intake manifold and block. And from what I ve heard if your car gets key'd the metal (on steel cars) will bend and fold before the paint even chips/cracks. Its the same paint they used to on the outside of Canada Place in Vancouver, its supposed to last 100 years without a noticable amount of fading.
Z||000005||anna||05-24-99||04:55 PM||||theogre.Im sure glad your satisfied with coming close on your paint.Close aint good enough for my cars,it has to be exactly the same.Also ,why would any body use a Spraycan for a little scratch,my opinon is that after a while you get a pretty good build up of paint. Overlord.I guess you're lucky.What's youre secret,to be able to drive down the Road for years and never have a Rock hit youre car?<br>Punkndrulic.I hope I spelled that right.You said some thing about Endura Pacific.Are you talking about the Plastic paint or the rubber kind.If the Paint is that great ,why won't they use it on cars.
Z||000006||theogre||05-24-99||10:21 PM||||if all your doing is spraying it on.... you're right... you'll get a mess. proper use of spray cans or guns isn't easy. and there are steps to do afterward if you don't want it to look like hell.<p>here is an extreamly tough paint they do use on cars, motor cycle frames, and boats. DuPont Imron. It's a 2 part polyurethane enamel. It's definatly not for the home painter.
Z||000007||Eric||05-25-99||05:17 PM||||I had to jump into this paint conversation.  The paint on both my bumpers is cracked (looks like spider webs).  I'm going to repaint them soon and was wondering if anyone knew the correct paint to use on the flexible surfaces.  By the way, the color is black.
Z||000008||Phil||05-26-99||04:54 AM||||Bumper black  flex paint avail at Pep Boys etc.
Z||000009||Punkndrublic||05-27-99||07:12 PM||||Anne,  I don't know how popular the company is, its based in Calgary and theres alot of body shops around here that use it, the guy who rebuilt my engine uses it exclusively on the parts he paints. As for the rest of the world I don't know if they are aware of the company and their paint. The documentation I have on it says its aliphatic polyurethane paint, and you need a different primer and topcoat if your going to use it on fexible substrates ie. Fiero body panels. I just bought the regular stuff to paint my intake and valve covers, and so far theres no problems, but then again I also had them glass beaded and painted them the next day.
Z||000010||theogre||05-27-99||07:35 PM||||DuPong Imron will work an Fiero's semi ridged pannels. It should work on the nose/tail facia to, but I've not been able to test it on that.<p>We used it on cars, motor cycles, even a couple boats. It's about the toughest paint I've ever seen. It's a bitch to paint with. You have to apply it just right and is will set in the cup if you take to long or add to much hardener.
Z||000011||theogre||05-27-99||07:39 PM||||thats cute.... pong..... DuPont Imron
